From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:29:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: apple-h2fmi: Discover and validate PPN package geometry

Query both PPN parameter pages before registering MTD devices. The measured
64 GB P105 has eight CAUs per bus with 128 pages per block; the imported
fixed geometry aliases addresses on that profile. Retain support for the
reference two-CAU package and reject unsupported or mismatched profiles.

Use four row address cycles for the supported PPN protocol. Check status
before requesting payload, restore the inherited controller state on every
exit, and stop I/O after a transport or cleanup failure. Report a terminal
error for a failed zero-byte MTD read so MEMREAD cannot repeat that page.
Keep page programming and capture interfaces outside this read change.

Add synthetic KUnit tests for parameter parsing and address uniqueness,
including offsets beyond 4 GiB and the context address view. A host harness
of the actual read functions passed 140146 ASan/UBSan assertions. Exact
current-base hardware qualification is pending.

Assisted-by: LLM
